<title>UK: Medison Co sets 44 million Sfr convertible bond.</title>
<headline>Medison Co sets 44 million Sfr convertible bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Credit Suisse First Boston.</p>
<p> BORROWER   MEDISON CORP LTD</p>
<p> AMT    44 MLN SFR    COUPON     0.25	MATURITY   *06.MAR.02</p>
<p> TYPE   CONVERTIBLE   ISS PRICE  100.0     PAY DATE    06.MAR.97</p>
<p> YIELD    **3.60	LISTING    NONE	DENOMS (K)  50</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   =</p>
<p> GOV LAW    SWISS     HOME CTRY  KOREA     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> NOTES     *PUTTABLE ON 06.MAR.00 AT 110.42. CALLABLE 06.MAR.99</p>
<p>		AND 06.MAR.00 AT 110.42, AND ON 06.MAR.01 AT 101.0</p>
<p>		SUBJECT TO 140 PCT RULE</p>
<p>	   **TO PUT</p>
<p>	     CONVERTIBLE INTO ORDINARY SHARES OF MEDISON CO LTD</p>
<p>	     FROM 07.APR.97 TO 06.FEB.02. CONVERSION PRICE IS</p>
<p>	     WON 123,410 PER SHARE. FOREX WON 595.44/1.00 SFR</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
